=== Phase 1 ===
Upon starting the fight, the Archive Guardian will:

* [[Flying (attribute)|Levitate in the air]], preventing non-halberd melee attacks from reaching it
* Initially target the first player in orb order, so the party leader should initiate the fight

==== Levitating ====
[[File:Archive Guardian - inert guardian destroy.mp4|thumb|400px|The tank focuses on the Guardian and clears mushrooms around it in preparation for meleeing the boss upon being grounded. Meanwhile, another player destroys an inert guardian, dealing significant damage.]]
While levitating, the boss primarily attacks with ranged, throwing rocks at players in front and within a 90 degree angle to its sides (TODO: There appears to be nuance to this in practice). During this ranged attack, its tendrils will also deal typeless damage to anyone standing behind it. It will also attack with melee if the player stands under it, and it is possible with some effort to lure the boss into using melee and take no damage by walking out before this occurs, but the timing for this is inconsistent.

Roughly every four attacks{{Clarify|Does not seem to be precisely four attacks and unclear if count is maintained between downs}}, '''Mushrooms''' will be spawned, explained in more detail below. 

Throughout this phase, [[Inert Guardian (Wall)|Inert Guardians]] can be charged to deal significant damage to the boss. This mechanic is discussed in more detail below.

Once the shield health is depleted, it will crash into the ground, where it may also be attacked with melee.

==== Grounded ====
[[File:Archive Guardian - meleeing.mp4|thumb|400px|Players ground the Archive Guardian and proceed to attack it with melee, circling around it to minimise vine lashes.]]
While grounded, after an initial 6 tick delay, the Archive Guardian will target players' locations with a tendril every 3 ticks. Tendrils will spawn one after another and attack on the same 3 tick cycle in a 3x3 AoE swipe around it, dealing moderate melee damage and attacking 3 times before disappearing. While grounded, its fire weakness goes from 80% down to 40%, so swapping to a melee weapon is highly recommended. Players who are using melee should try to run in sync to avoid colliding with the surrounding tiles. Praying [[Protect from Melee]] reduces the maximum damage to 11. Tendrils always spawn on the side of you opposite the boss. If the boss is west of you, tendrils spawn east of you. If you start far away from the boss, you only need to move 1 tile towards the boss to avoid tendrils and prevent the room from being filled with them.

After 34 ticks, or upon reaching 33% health, the boss will again begin to levitate. If above 33% health the '''Phase 1''' cycle continues as defined above, but now targeting the next player in the orb order; if at or below 33% health, '''Phase 2''' begins immediately as below.

=== Phase 2 ===
After reaching 33% health, the Guardian immediately begins flying and switches to alternating between '''Mushrooms''' and a magic-based "laser" attack, respectively. 

The laser attack is indicated by the message {{mes|The Archive Guardian focuses intently on [player name]/[you]!}} targeting a random player and dealing fatal damage if there are more than 2 players alive and it is not reduced. Its damage can be reduced by players standing on the same tile or line as the target player. Alternatively, the laser can be tick-eaten. A visual cue for when to heal is to click as soon as the laser appears in front of the boss.

Praying Protect from Magic reduces the laser's damage slightly.

'''Inert Guardians''' can also be hit by the laser beam, charging it fully, and after a short delay, dealing damage to the Guardian's shield or health in this phase. This is discussed in further detail below.

[[Vengeance]] does apply from melee hits from step-unders, the ranged rocks, tentacles and the laser. As a strat: the laser can be solo tanked at high HP with a tick-eat and protect from magic disabled for maximum value. [[Vengeance Other]] can also be considered and whether to use it on the shield vs the boss's actual HP. [[Phoenix necklace|Phoenix Necklaces]] could be worn here during the tick-eat using same logic as tick-eat from [[Sotetseg|Sotetseg's]] Death Ball attack to heal without the use of brews/hard food.

=== Mushrooms ===
Throughout the entire fight, the Archive Guardian will periodically spawn two mushrooms near every player in the room. {{Ticks|5}} after spawning, if any player is within one tile of a mushroom it will explode and damage all players within a two tile radius, as follows:

* Players within '''one''' tile of a mushroom as it explodes, will 
** Take 10 damage 
** Be [[poison]]ed starting at 10 damage (or have their poison immunity removed)
** Have their run disabled 
** If the player was not immune to poison, they will become drowsy and become forced to walk for several seconds as well as suffering prayer drain.
* Players within '''two''' tiles of a mushroom as it explodes will take 3-4 damage with no other effects. 

Running adjacent to a mushroom, then immediately two tiles away will "pop" it, dealing no damage to the player (note: any other nearby players within two tiles of the mushroom as it "pops" will still take damage as defined above). Wearing a [[serpentine helm]] will not reduce any damage, but will prevent players from being poisoned as well as allowing players to re-activate run immediately.

=== Inert Guardians ===
[[File:Archive Guardian - phase 2 hyper beam.mp4|thumb|400px|In order to maximise damage dealt to its actual health, the team stops attacking the boss after its shield health reaches just under 40%, and has its beam attack fire toward an inert guardian.]]
Around the room are four inert guardians, which can be charged by attacking them. Two guardians are accessible by melee, a third can only be targeted with ranged or magic (earth weakness) attacks, and a fourth cannot be damaged by players but is susceptible to the Guardian's '''Phase 2''' laser attack. Due to their -4 flat armour and incredibly low defence, they are an effective way of breaking through the Guardian's shield.

Fully charging an inert guardian deals damage equivalent to ~40% of the Guardian's shield. During '''Phase 1''', this damage will only effect the shield health. However, if the shield is broken by an inert guardian during '''Phase 2''', any overflow damage will be dealt as physical damage to the Guardian, up to 15% of its health. During phase 2, fully charging a guardian will deal damage equal to 15% of the Guardian's health.

A useful tactic during '''Phase 2''' is to keep the boss as close to, but below, 40% shield health before having the boss destroy an inert guardian with its laser, thus reducing the boss's non-shield health significantly.

===Defence Reduction===
The Archive Guardian's Defence level of 260 can be reduced to a minimum of 156 (<math>260 \times 0.6 = 156</math>).{{CiteNews|url=https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/the-fractured-archive---out-today?oldschool=1|title=The Fractured Archive - Out Today|newsdate=21 October 2026|quote=The following NPCs should have a 60% cap on their Defence Reduction, meaning an NPC with 100 Defence could have it reduced down to 60, but no further: Archive Guardian, Bork, Ezekiel, Moia, Xarth, Ocellus}}

The Archive Guardian recalculates its base levels depending on the damage dealt during the downed phase:
* Defence = 260 - (130 * damage / grounded_base_hp)
* Magic = 250 + (125 * damage / grounded_base_hp)

If defence reducing special attacks were used, the boss will take the lower value when updating.

