=== Phase 1 ===
The first player to enter the room becomes the '''tank''' until they die. On death, the next player in orb order becomes the tank.

Ezekiel attacks twice with '''Cleave''' followed by his '''Flying Swords''' mechanic. He repeats this pattern indefinitely throughout '''phase 1.''' 

==== Cleave ====
Ezekiel's melee attacks '''cleave''' almost completely around him, with the central three tiles opposite of him being safe from the melee attacks. If he is facing north, then the tiles south of his hitbox (barring corners) are safe. Teammates should attempt to stay opposite of the tank, or step one tile back during his attack, to avoid damage. '''Protect from Melee''' reduces damage taken for the tank, but every other player will still take significant melee damage.

If Ezekiel is unable to attack his target with his cleave melee, he will use a strong magic attack on all players in the arena. There is a chance for Ezekiel to mark another player as the tank after using this magic attack.

==== Flying Swords ====
After a short pause following his second cleave attack, Ezekiel will perform a large cross-shaped AoE lightning attack centred on him, which will burst twice before disappearing. The bursts are two ticks apart, so it is possible to attack Ezekiel in between them if timed correctly. The lightning attack can be dodged by moving diagonally or in an L-movement away from Ezekiel when you see his overhead text<!-- what's his overhead text here? --> telegraphing the attack.

Ezekiel will then spawn three to four [[Animated Sword|Animated Swords]], in one of a fixed number of patterns. These can be [[The Fractured Archive/Strategies#Perfect dodges|perfectly dodged]] similar to Drakan's attacks in [[The Blood Moon Rises]] — stand in the way of the attack, then move out of the way on the same tick as the attack. This can be timed by the countdown above the swords: clicking as soon as the bar empties will time the dodge perfectly. If done correctly, your character will dodge roll out of the attack. You can still dodge roll if you were moving or attacking with ranged on the tick before. Each perfect dodge rewards 5% special attack energy.

Swords always fly in a straight line. If there are 4 swords, they will always fly at the same time. If there are 3, they will fly one at a time, 1 tick apart.

If Ezekiel is '''completely hit by a sword''' (i.e. the sword and Ezekiel's 3x3 hitbox, or SW tile is perfectly aligned), he will take damage and be stunned for a few seconds. A successful hit will result in him yelling {{overhead|Argh!}}. If he is not successfully hit, he will instead say {{overhead|Saradomin, give me strength.}} and heal for a large amount of health.

Hitting the swords increases their damage by the amount dealt to the sword (indicated by the yellow bar), up to a maximum of 80 extra damage. The swords have a 100% elemental weakness to air spells, and resist Ranged attacks. Note that empowering the swords increases the damage they deal to both Ezekiel '''as well as to the player, though damage dealt to the player is capped to 70.'''<gallery mode="packed" heights="200" style="text-align:left">
Ezekiel - animated swords 3.mp4|Ezekiel animates four swords, with three rows of safe tiles to stand on. The grey marked tiles visible represent the boss arena's boundaries.
Ezekiel - animated swords 2.mp4|Ezekiel animates three swords on one side. A player stands in the centre of the middle sword's path so that they can react to the other two swords' movements.
Ezekiel - animated swords 1.mp4|Ezekiel animates four swords surrounding the area, with the tank positioning Ezekiel to get struck by one, as well as to dodge it.
</gallery>

===Phase 2===
[[File:Ezekiel - phase 2 dodging.mp4|thumb|450px|Players perfectly dodging Ezekiel's lightning attacks during the second phase of the fight by seeking out the swords that were not struck by lightning.]]
Upon reaching less than 33% of his health, Ezekiel will reposition himself to a side of the arena, dropping a large amount of swords that will force the player(s) into the remaining 3x3 space in the middle of the room. He will then imbue himself with magic and summon three more swords, one each to his left, right and front. Ezekiel reduces incoming damage in this phase, but takes more damage as his health decreases.

====Lightning patterns====
During this phase, Ezekiel repeats a lightning pattern three times in a row:
*Three shapes appear in a '''V''' under Ezekiel, and two of them are struck by lightning.
*The pattern tells you which direction to dodge inside the '''3x3 grid''' the player is placed in.
*Each of the three dodges restores special attack energy when timed correctly, similar to the animated swords.

