===Bork===
Bork attacks with AoE-based melee, launching shockwaves around him by beating his drum. Additionally, he has 8 [[flat armour]] and 2 [[Magic resistance]], meaning that all melee and ranged attacks are reduced by 8 and magic attacks by 2. For every 25% damage dealt to the Smorks, Bork's flat armour increases by 2, up to a maximum of 14 flat armour. Bork is weakest to both crush and heavy ranged attacks.

Bork will target the first player who enters the arena, chasing after them. If his target is not within melee range he will generate a stronger wave on his first attack, which covers up to three tiles from him. The second attack will only affect the tiles immediately around him. Bork will periodically change aggression, indicated with him yelling {{Overhead|Bork smash [player name] now.}} Protect from Melee will reduce some damage from his attacks.

===The Smorks===
The Smorks attack with both ranged and magic; ranged attacks are indicated with a cluster of farming tools and magic attacks are indicated as a cluster of potions. These attacks cannot be tick eaten. These are launched on all players that are not focused by Bork if there are two or more players present in the arena. Alongside these attacks, the Smorks will launch incendiary and heavy cannonballs. The Smorks are static, in the centre of the arena and block Bork's beats. They are weakest to heavy ranged attacks.

===Cannonballs===
====Incendiary cannonballs====
Incendiary cannonballs will deal heavy damage if caught in its AoE and leave behind splatters of oil, which if stepped on will deal 6-7 damage per tick and ignite the player, inflicting a burn that starts at 2 damage. If Bork is hit by one he will take 25-30 damage.

====Heavy cannonballs====
[[File:Bork and the Smorks - flinching setup.mp4|thumb|450px|The non-tanks positions themselves behind the tank, allowing the tank to position Bork to be flinched upon getting stunned. Bork's hitboxes is placed perpendicular to the Smorks, allowing the team to flinch Bork during the counter stomps.]]
Heavy cannonballs will be indicated with the Smorks yelling for Bork to avoid it. If the cannonball lands on Bork, he will become dazed, and the Smorks will temporarily stop attacking. This will lift his damage reduction and all melee attacks on him are dealt as [[successful hit]]s for a short time.

====Stomp====
After recovering, or if the cannonball did not hit him, Bork will stomp several times, indicated by {{Overhead|Bork very angry!}} (if hit), {{Overhead|Bork crush now.}} or {{Overhead|Bork think it stomp time now!}} (if not hit) covering the entire arena. These stomps will deal much more damage than Bork's drumbeats, even with Protect from Melee active. These can be avoided by hiding behind the Smorks' cart.

===Bork tank positioning===
====Tank role====
The first player to enter the arena will initiate tanking and needs to pray melee. Tank should run to Bork and wait until Smorks shoots his heavy cannonball, the second of the two specials. At that point, the entire team will want to walk back two tiles to lure Bork into the heavy cannonball for a stun. If the tank stands on the central tile of the Smorks prior to the heavy cannonball shot, Bork will be stunned on a tile that allows the team to flinch Bork during the stun phase.

After Bork is stunned by the cannonball and the punish cycle is complete, he will do an overhead call out that names the next player who needs to tank and the cycle will continue. Bork will remember his last four targets before he may attempt to select them again, provided that they are in the arena. In a 2-man encounter, where player A is picked first, he will mark them as a target again after player B has finished tanking.

====Non-tank role====
At the start of a new tank cycle, it's ideal for the players not tanking to lure the incendiary cannonball shot away from the tank (position so that the incendiary shot hits Bork to deal true damage). Afterwards, the non-tanking players can stand behind the tank to give the tank an easy way to lure Bork into the heavy cannonball for a stun.

===Attack speed===
As the health of the Smorks lowers, Bork will begin to beat his drum faster, subsequently causing both enemies' attack speed to increase.

===Enrage phase===
When one of the pair is killed, the other will become enraged and initiate the second half of the fight.

*If Bork is killed first, the Smorks' attack speed will significantly increase and their attacks will hit everyone in the arena, though incendiary cannonballs are still launched at one player. The damage from their auto-attacks are increased.
*If the Smorks are killed first, Bork will begin stomping the entire arena for heavy melee damage.

