=== Undead Binders ===
Moia will start the fight by summoning several [[undead binder]]s that stand evenly spaced in the arena, leaving one gap for players to start in. Binders shuffle around the arena every 15 ticks, and will attack anyone within two tiles of them with melee; the damage can be fully mitigated with Protect from Melee, however it is not recommended to do this unless multiple binders are able to attack the player at once. If a player stands underneath a binder after the shuffle, they will be pushed out and take minor damage.

Moia continually respawns binders throughout the fight; killing them will allow for more space to reposition without being attacked, and make the fight more manageable. Despite being undead, [[Crumble Undead]] does not work on them.

=== Magic Attack ===
After 3-4 ranged attacks Moia will teleport to another side of her arena and launch a slow blue projectile that deals magic damage. Moia will also launch a ranged attack during this time. The ranged attack '''will hit first''' despite being launched second. Once this ranged attack hits, there is a 2 tick delay before the magic attack registers, so once the ranged attack hits, swap to Protect from Magic to block the magic attack.

=== Cough ===
After 2 magic attacks, she will target a player with a smoke cloud projectile that will infect them with a cough that continuously applies poison multiple times. If a player is not poisoned, the initial poison damage is 2 but it will quickly ramp up to 5, 13, and up to 20 damage in addition to draining prayer points if left uncured. A player can reset the poison damage by curing it anytime and damage from this coughing is significantly mitigated by wearing a [[Serpentine helm]]. The player hit by the virus should avoid standing next to other teammates or undead binders, as this will spread the virus and can deal immense damage over time if they are not dealt with properly. The initial cough impact does not spread to other players; therefore players can stand together as the cough begins while the targeted player leaves the group within 8 ticks before the next cough. After the 4th cough, the poison effect will clear from the player regardless of any antipoison being used.

=== Enrage ===
Upon reaching 33% of her health, Moia will enter enrage. She will heal all binders to full health, and reposition the binders into a diamond formation around her. 10 ticks after healing the undead binders, she will consume the skeleton in the middle of the room and heal herself for that binder's current health, plus an additional 80 HP if one was consumed (the amount depends on the raid scale). During the transition, a zombie can spawn under the player and be eligible to melee the player before moving in formation. When Moia disappears, you can safely pray melee against a zombie and burst it down to make space.

When Moia reappears for enrage, switch back to protect from ranged. An additional countdown bar below her health bar will begin ticking down. If any binders are left alive when the timer runs out, she will deal roughly 25 damage to all of the players in the arena per undead binder alive. If all binders are successfully defeated when the timer is up, she will spawn another set and continue charging subsequent attacks until she is defeated. Each subsequent charge has a shorter and shorter timer (estimated to be 40 ticks for first countdown, and gets shorter by 5t each time).

A [[venator bow]] is highly recommended to attack multiple binders mid-shuffle, whenever they position closely in the middle of the arena, or for Moia's enrage phase. During the first set of undead binders, players can venator bow Moia for extra damage with bounces from the binders. Subsequent sets of binders might require focusing on the binders as the timer counts down.

