Dreadnoth moves slowly around the arena, around one tile every two ticks. He primarily attacks with melee, which will hit everyone around him, so it is recommended to range or mage him from afar. Dreadnoth is considered a demon, however he has 75% demonbane resistance, making them significantly less effective than other options. Additionally, he has 85% susceptibility to [[fire spells]] and 40% freeze resistance. The [[Scorching bow]] special attack can also be used to root him in place.

Once Dreadnoth reaches 85%, 65% and 45% of his max health he will do an arena-wide slam, followed by three ranged attacks. Ensure Protect from Melee is active for the slam, and Protect from Range is active for the projectiles. Each sequential slam phase will have an additional slam, up to three. Every slam will be followed by three ranged attacks. This will also spawn a lot of [[Jelly (Dreadnoth)|jellies]] that also attack with melee. These must be killed as soon as possible as they will drain prayer with each attack made. [[Chinchompa|Chinchompas]], [[Ice Barrage]], [[Blood Barrage]], or the [[Venator bow]] can be used to kill them quickly. In large groups, it is easier to stack together during this phase to ensure all jellies can be killed together.

When jellies die, and periodically through the fight, jelly will spawn on tiles. This will deal 6-8 damage per tick when stepped on.
When the boss reaches 25% health, he will announce '''{{Overhead|*glub glub*}}''' and begin to jump towards and slam on a random player. This will do large amounts of damage and heal the boss (~30-40) if the player is underneath Dreadnoth. All players should swap to Protect from Melee before the slam, as this slam is identically similar to the ones used earlier. Following the slam, two projectiles; one ranged and one jelly splatter, will target the player, so it is important to keep moving. If there are any jellies still alive, if Dreadnoth jumps and slams on top of them, he absorbs them and heals as they combine. Since Dreadnoth no longer uses his normal melee attack during enrage, players can take advantage with melee, provided that there is enough space to safely move around.

On death, the boss will explode and spawn roughly seven jellies with 50% health. Once these jellies are killed, the encounter ends.

