The fight consists of the team fighting a [[Dagon'hai Elder]] and two [[Dagon'hai Monk]]s. Upon entering the arena, the elder will order the ritual to start while he deals with the interlopers, and the two monks will quickly scatter to the sides to research the tomes scattered across several desks.

The elder and monks share the same health pool and base stats, but defence reduction is not shared. Therefore, prioritise one Dagon'hai to apply defence reduction and focus on them unless another Dagon'hai has been stunned from countering their elemental channel.

In the centre of the arena is a cauldron in which the trio maintain their ritual. This cauldron will periodically move around the centre tiles, and running into it will shove the player away for up to 9 damage.

The elder attacks with ranged and magic; the ranged attacks consist of a grey projectile, while the magic attacks are surge spells. These attacks deal damage on impact and can be prayed against with slow reactions. He will focus on one player, but his attacks will also hit other players within three tiles of them. By spreading out, other players will not be hit by his attacks.

Throughout the fight, both the elder and monks will attempt to finish the ritual. The monks may either attempt to siphon knowledge from the books into the cauldron in the centre of the arena, or channel a spell. The elder will only channel spells into the cauldron. The ritual's progression is indicated with a yellow bar underneath the cauldron's health bar, with each successful charge increasing its bar by 25%. If this fills completely, the Dagon'hai will empower themselves; all three will gain a set amount of health <!--maybe tied to amount of successful disruptions--> and start attacking the team. This will likely result in a wipe, as the elder will attack all players in the arena with a barrage of empowered surge spells (with each attack consisting of two surges) that deal significant damage through prayer.

*'''Elemental Channel:''' The elder or monk will yell one of the following, which is interrupted by casting the corresponding elemental spell on them. '''Players can splash if their magic accuracy is not high enough''' (exact value unknown). A yellow bar will appear over their shield bar, which indicates charge progression. If the cast is successfully interrupted, the spell is guaranteed to deal a maximum hit and the Dagon'hai will be briefly stunned, taking 15% more damage while disoriented.
**'''{{Overhead|I'll feed the flames!}}:''' Cast a fire spell on the elder or monk attempting to channel energy.
**'''{{Overhead|I'll guide the flow!}}:''' Cast a water spell on the elder or monk attempting to channel energy.
**'''{{Overhead|I'll focus the winds!}}:''' Cast an air spell on the elder or monk attempting to channel energy.
**'''{{Overhead|I'll strengthen the bond!}}:''' Cast an earth spell on the elder or monk attempting to channel energy.
*'''Tome Empowerment:''' One of the monks will yell a corresponding quote, and air gusts will appear indicating the tiles a player needs to stand on in order to block a projectile to which would cause one of three effects around the arena. Prior to this occurring, the monk will say {{Overhead|What have we here?}}. A successful block will result in the monk yelling {{Overhead|Curse you!}}
**'''Zamorak:''' The monk will yell {{Overhead|Zamorak empowers us!}} If blocked, the player will be hit by the energy, dealing ~25 damage and causing fireballs to launch in a 7x7 AoE around them, with one on the tile they were on. This also inflicts a burn starting at 3 damage. If not blocked, the cauldron will instantly damage everyone and then spew fireballs in a large area.
**'''Bandos:''' The monk will yell {{Overhead|Bandosian strength, feed the flame!}} If blocked, the player will be hit by the energy, dealing up to 55 damage and causing a shockwave that spreads out on an eight tile range from them. The shockwaves will not damage the player who took the hit, however it will hit other players multiple times if they improperly run out. If not blocked, all players will take heavy damage and a shockwave will erupt from the cauldron.
**'''Saradomin:''' The monk will yell {{Overhead|Saradominist zeal, feed the flame!}} If blocked, the player will be healed ~10 to 20 hp, and cause blue and yellow shadows to appear around the arena, which summons lightning strikes after a short delay. Stepping on the yellow lightning strikes will restore health and prayer to players, note that if a yellow strike spawns in the middle it will be covered by the cauldron therein becoming unreachable.
*** If not blocked, there will still be lightning strikes, however all players will also be healed ~50 hp. This means that players should allow the Saradominist spell to be channeled to heal teammates (especially for those who've tanked Bandosian and Zamorakian spells), provided that it will not complete the ritual (yellow bar).
<gallery mode="packed" heights="200" style="text-align:left">
The Dagon'hai - Zamorakian spell.mp4|The team successfully disrupts a Zamorakian spell.
The Dagon'hai - Bandosian spell.mp4|A player successfully disrupts a Bandosian spell, with their teammate far enough to avoid the resulting shockwave.
The Dagon'hai - Saradominist spell.mp4|The team allows a Saradominist spell to be channeled, resulting in significant healing. 
</gallery>

Once the health bar of the three enemies are fully depleted, the Dagon'hai will channel Zamorak's energy to protect themselves and restore their shield gauge to full, which in turn causes the ritual's stability to drop 20%. When this occurs, two or three portals will appear, dropping three or two [[Imp (Dagon'hai Trio)|imps]] each into the arena. The portals have a yellow bar over them, indicating progress for an imp to be summoned. If the player is next to the portal, they will drain its health at the cost of prayer points and preventing imps from spawning in. The imps attack with melee, with the damage being reduced with Protect from Melee. Players will always land successful and maximum hits on imps. Killing an imp will empower the player, allowing their next attack to deal 33% more damage. This additively stacks alongside the 15% from attacking a stunned Dagon'hai to deal very high damage.

After depleting the mages' shield gauge the fifth time, the ritual will become unstable and the cauldron will explode, killing one of the monks instantly, while the elder and the remaining monk will be stunned. The elder will quickly recover, however both enemies have 7 health and are easily dispatched by any weapon. If any imps are somehow remaining after the Dagon'hai are eliminated, they will despawn once the room is considered cleared.

