===Phase 1===
[[File:Xarth - phase 1 tanking.mp4|thumb|450px|Players designate a tank for phase 1 (usually orb order), and then avoid the incoming explosion by hiding behind the pillars.]]
Xarth attacks exclusively with magic during this phase, prioritising the player closest to him. He also has a shield that mitigates some incoming damage. Successful magic attacks will result in a burn that will reset and stack on successive hits. Players should be mindful of how many attacks they take as taking a lot will result in severe burn damage.

On a fixed timer (after 5 magic attacks), he will bind all players and launch two searing projectiles while charging up an explosive blast in the process. Once the projectiles are launched, immediately hide behind the pillar. After the first explosion, his shield is removed. If all players go behind the pillar too fast, Xarth will do AoE blast damaging everyone.

It is important that all members stand behind one pillar and path the same direction to it, as improper pathing and positioning can result in multiple pillars being destroyed, leaving them open to subsequent blasts.

In a pinch, a player can act as a pillar. They will take the full ~45 damage and those behind will take ~7. Players cannot stand on top of each other, or they will all take full damage. This tactic can also be used during phase 2. The explosion can be recoiled with [[Vengeance]].

When DD'ing at certain scales (e.g. 5) he will never attack one player. this seems to be randomly decided each raid. The randomly chosen 'non tank' can choose to stand in front of the DD to tank a few hits to save others some health.

===Phase 2===
[[File:Xarth - phase 2 melee.mp4|thumb|450px|A player freezes the incoming corpses right before they can heal Xarth, allowing designated teammates to attack him and the corpses with a venator bow. Another player is assigned to attack Xarth with melee.]]
When all pillars are gone, Xarth will initiate the second phase of the fight. He will launch several flames into the arena, serving as hazards that will deal damage and inflict burns if stepped on. These flames will periodically spread to adjacent tiles throughout the fight, slowly filling the room. He will no longer use magic attacks, instead swapping to ranged and melee, though he remains static in the centre of the arena. Xarth's ranged attacks damage on impact, meaning that they can be blocked even with slow reactions. The ranged attacks are fully blocked with Protect from Ranged, while the melee attacks can deal significant damage through melee. While he is weaker to crush attacks, players who are using melee should flinch him, attacking after his ranged attacks to avoid getting hit by melee.

Throughout the phase, he will additionally reanimate [[Corpse (Xarth)|corpses]], indicated with him using his magic attack animation. These corpses will spawn from the edges of the arena and will approach him, similar to [[sleepwalker]]s at [[The Nightmare]]. If allowed to reach him, they will heal him for their remaining health. Corpses can be frozen, or they may be attacked with [[water spells]] to douse them, making them pause briefly and take guaranteed max hits from melee and light ranged attacks. [[Undead Grasp]], under the effects of [[Mark of Darkness]], freezes corpses in place for 24 ticks. Ice, water spells, and Undead Grasp do not have any delay when used on corpses. Avoid using fire spells, as this will cause him to summon more corpses.

To guarantee a freeze or grasp on the [[Corpse (Xarth)|corpses]], you need at least the Magic attack bonus listed below. The [[Ice ancient sceptre]] lowers this requirement because of its passive 10% accuracy bonus to [[ice spells]] when casting against unfrozen targets.
