===Phase 1===
[[File:Ocellus - phase 1 movement.mp4|thumb|450px|Players fighting Ocellus during phase 1 of the fight, using precise movements to block his charging attack.]]
During this phase, Ocellus is weakest to light and heavy ranged attacks. He also possesses a shield which must be depleted to progress to the next phase.

Ocellus will begin the fight by moving to each corner, attacking with ranged (orange) and magic (blue) projectiles. While walking to a quadrant, he will have [[Protect from Melee]] active. Once a quadrant is reached, he will summon seven tendrils, one at a time towards him. These tendrils will channel energy into him, which can be mitigated by standing on them. The player will take some damage, but gain "healing charges". When attacking, these charges will be expended and the player will be healed proportional to charges consumed. After the seventh tendril, Ocellus will slam the area around him, covering a two tile range and dealing up to 35 damage if caught in one.

At 66% and 25% shield durability, Ocellus will teleport to the centre of the arena and spawn two tendrils in a clockwise direction, with the same two tile AoE blast after the second tendril. He will do this four times. After this attack is complete, he will charge up a powerful attack based on the energy he accumulated. If not enough tendrils were mitigated, he will announce {{Overhead|Embrace... annihilation...}}, launching numerous projectiles that deal over 80+ damage in total, having a very high chance to kill players. If enough were mitigated, he will instead announce {{Overhead|Death... awaits...}}, launching one projectile that deals 17-18 damage.

