| weapon2 = {{plink|Ascension crossbows}} > {{plink|Twisted bow}} / {{plink|Toxic blowpipe}}
| weapon3 = {{plink|Scythe of Vitur}} / {{plink|Inquisitor's mace}} > {{plink|Soulreaper axe}}
| weapon4 = {{plink|Emberlight}} > {{plink|Abyssal bludgeon}} / {{plink|Zamorakian hasta}}
}}

Before the shield is fully depleted, the team should decide on which quadrant to stand on as this will influence the start of phase 3.

===Phase 2===
[[File:Ocellus - phase 2 portal skipping.mp4|thumb|450px|A player performs the portal skip technique during phase 2 of the fight.]]
Once his shield is reduced to 0, Ocellus will teleport to the center of the arena and create 4 quadrants surrounded by orange and purple portals. Here, players must attack Ocellus via disrupting [[the Blade]]. 

Ocellus' defensive values will change once this phase occurs; he will gain 35 Defence levels, and he becomes weakest to crush, followed by heavy ranged attacks. Due to needing to constantly reposition yourself around the room, melee and fast ranged weapons are much more difficult to use. Defence can be significantly drained during this phase as well.

Purple portals will spawn damaging attacks, while 2 orange portals will spawn on either side that intersect in a safe zone; this pattern is not random and is the same for every fight. After five sets of attacks, purple damaging pools will spawn on the floor of the arena followed by an orange portal. This will allow players to teleport to a new quadrant and avoid the incoming barrage of attacks as the quadrant becomes unsafe.

The Blade stores damage dealt during this phase and releases it at the end of each quadrant, however only half of all damage dealt will transfer to the next phase.

The portals can be skipped over with precise movement and timing, as seen in the demonstration.

{{Recommended equipment
| style = [[File:Ocellus icon.png]] Ocellus Phase 2
| weapon1 = {{plink|Twisted bow}}
| weapon2 = {{plink|Zaryte crossbow}}
| weapon3 = {{plink|Armadyl crossbow}} > {{plink|Dragon crossbow}}
| weapon4 = {{plink|Scorching bow}}
}}

===Phase 3===
Ocellus will destroy parts of the arena to create 4 diagonal quadrants, separated by floating rocks that can be jumped across.

Ocellus' defence values change again in this phase. He is still weakest to crush attacks (though he gains some crush defence), and his range defence significantly increases without any specific ranged style weakness.<!-- Meta is to start with bandos or arma censer so maul/ralos maxes. Not sure where to add this --> 

Ocellus will choose a player to focus on in each quadrant, known as the tank. His choice is based on orb order, going down the player list when a quadrant is cleared or when the tank dies. The party leader begins as the tank for the first quadrant (unless they died earlier), the second alive player in orb order is the tank for the second quadrant, and so forth. The designated tank will have a unique sound played to them, and a chat message indicates which player Ocellus is focusing on.

Ocellus takes 10% extra damage from players standing directly opposite the tank. See [[#Bonus damage from the mirrored tile|below]] for details.

At the end of each quadrant, Ocellus will announce {{Overhead|Obliteration...}} or {{Overhead|Run... It matters not...}} and begin charging a blast that will destroy the quadrant. The player must '''quickly''' run to the next quadrant before the charge finishes, jumping on the sets of rocks to the next quadrant (starting with the leftmost rock first, and working their way to the right). If the player is still on the platform when it is destroyed, '''they will be instantly killed'''. The rocks will collapse shortly after the quadrant, and will likewise kill players still on them.

==== Mechanics ====
At the start of the first three quadrants, persistent void pools spawn underneath all players except for the tank, dealing periodic damage when stepped in. These pools can be stacked; if the non-tank players stand on one tile, their pools will all be placed on that tile, and only one void pool will spawn per quadrant. This leaves the floor much less cluttered and makes other mechanics significantly easier. It is recommended to coordinate the chosen pile tiles with your team beforehand (preferably on out of the way edge tiles).

Ocellus will pursue the tank with melee. If he is unable to reach the tank, he will attack with a powerful spread void shot that deals 20+ damage to each player.

Ocellus' attack pattern is 2 melee attacks, followed by a dodgeable directional wave attack that travels across the arena. After every two attack cycles, Ocellus will use one of three special attacks. He also periodically uses two secondary effects, Void Spawns and Void Vine.

[[File:Ocellus - phase 3 melee sweep and triple charged blade.mp4|thumb|450px|Ocellus will start with two melee attacks, followed by a sweeping attack. After two of these, he will unleash a special attack; in this clip, he performs the charged blade attack three times.]]

===== Secondary Attacks =====
* '''Void Vine.''' Ocellus will say {{overhead|Your panic... is futile...}}, {{overhead|Await... the void...}}, or {{Overhead|The void... will take you...}}, then root 1 player with a [[Void Vine]] that can only be attacked directly by another player. Failure to break the vine in time will deal upwards of 50 damage.
** The player can break themselves free with a venator bow, or with barrage spells/chinchompas if the player is next to Ocellus' southwest tile.
* '''Void Spawns.''' Ocellus spawns a set of Voids (different in every quadrant). Failure to kill them will damage all players. These Void spawns empower the player who kills them. Each type of Void can be max hit by a corresponding style, though the player must have enough corresponding accuracy bonus to guarantee this max hit.
** [[Void Siphon|Void Siphons]] shoot healing projectiles towards Ocellus. These can be blocked by standing between them and the boss, healing the player for 6 Hitpoints each. Killing the void siphon heals the slayer for 22 Hitpoints. These will be max hit by Ranged Attacks.
** [[Void Augmenter|Void Augmenters]] will boost your combat stats when killed. These will be max hit by Magic Attacks. Note: These require a relatively high magic accuracy to max hit on them. Void Augmenters have an earth weakness, and can be one-shot by Earth Surge with +9% magic strength (though one must meet the accuracy requirement).
** [[Void Rift|Void Rifts]] will reset your attack cooldown when killed. These will be max hit by Melee, Ranged, and Magic, but Magic Attacks require the same magic accuracy as Void Augmenters. Void Rifts also have the same earth weakness as Void Augmenters.

===== Special Attacks =====
[[File:Ocellus - phase 3 untether.mp4|thumb|450px|Ocellus begins his untether attack, with the player demonstrating the correct timing to avoid both parts of the attack.]]
* '''Prayer'''. Ocellus spins around with his blade, hitting every player in the quadrant and forming a void pool underneath him. <!--Protect from melee blocks all damage from the spin. -->Afterwards, the void pool will pulse outwards in a purple flash<!--, indicating the last moment to deactivate overhead prayers--> before forming into a circular sawblade and exploding. While this is happening, falling Debris will target each player's location, dealing damage on impact and leaving behind a temporary damaging area. The <!--purple pulse/-->sawblade explosion is repeated an additional time for each quadrant destroyed, capping out at three total explosions per special during the third quadrant. 
: To avoid this attack, pray protect from melee for the initial spin, then deactivate your overhead (3 tick window, purple pulse indicates the last chance to deactivate), then '''reactivate''' protect from melee as the sawblade pattern starts forming underneath Ocellus (1 tick window). Dodge the falling Debris while flicking your overheads. If overhead prayers are not manually deactivated in time, Ocellus will disable them and briefly prevent them from being reactivated, forcing you to tank the upcoming explosion (if this happens, you will get the overhead back in time for the second/third explosions.)
* '''Untether'''. Ocellus will say {{Overhead|Untether...}} and then float in the air, unable to be reached by melee attacks. Damaging purple portals will begin spawning on the ground, and the boss will continue attacking with magic. The entire ground will eventually erupt in a void attack, dealing 40+ damage. To avoid this, stand underneath the boss (inside the purple lines). The border will glow brighter twice before the attack commences and Ocellus will slam inside this safe area, dealing a similar amount of damage. Time your escape on the final glow of the purple border to avoid both attacks simultaneously.
* '''Insolence'''. Ocellus will announce {{Overhead|Insolence...}}. He will target 3 random players in series and send wide wave attacks at them, similar to earlier wave attacks. These are much larger and leave a lasting damaging field behind them.

==== Censers ====
The four censers around the room become active during this phase. Interacting with them provides certain benefits:
*[[Bandosian Censer]] - +Melee damage - Guaranteed accuracy and max hit on your next melee attack. It also reduces the attack cooldown for the next hit.
*[[Armadylean Censer]] - +Ranged damage - Guaranteed accuracy and max hit on your next ranged attack. It also reduces the attack cooldown for the next hit.
*[[Zarosian Censer]] - Special attack - Restores 50% of your special attack energy.
*[[Saradomin Censer]] - Healing - Restores 40 Hitpoints and 40 prayer points.

==== Attack Rotation ====
The phase 3 attack pattern repeats as follows:
* '''Attack cycle''': Attack → Attack → Directional wave attack

Ocellus performs two attack cycles between each special attack. The specials rotate in this order:

{| class="wikitable"
! Order !! Preceded by !! Special attack
|-
| 1 || 2 attack cycles || '''Prayer special'''
|-
| 2 || 2 attack cycles || '''Untether'''
|-
| 3 || 2 attack cycles || '''Prayer special'''
|-
| 4 || 2 attack cycles || '''Insolence'''
|}

The order then repeats from the start. The order continues across platforms: for example, if the last special attack was Untether, the first special attack performed on the next platform will be the Prayer special, then the Insolence special and so forth. An exception is if the quadrant is phased early, before Ocellus performs a non-Prayer special attack, in which case that non-Prayer special is skipped altogether. e.g If the first quadrant is destroyed after the ''first'' Prayer special, the next special attacks will be Prayer followed by ''Insolence (''instead of Untether). If the second quadrant is again phased after the following Prayer special, the next special attack on the third quadrant will once again be Insolence. <!-- I'm a little confused. By the skip logic, wouldn't this skip Insolence and go back to Untether? --> This effectively skips untether for the entire encounter.{{fact}}

Secondary mechanic spawns seem to follow these rules:

* First Auto attack on the second and third platform will be paired with a void rift/augmenter/siphon.
* First Auto attack after the first Prayer special will be paired with root.
* First Auto after any special, except during root, is paired with voids. If the boss phased during either special, a void will spawn on the first hit on the next platform. {{fact}}
* There's a chance the voids will spawn on the 2nd attack of the 2nd attack cycle after roots. {{fact}}

==== Bonus damage from the mirrored tile ====
Ocellus takes an extra 10% damage from attacks made from directly opposite the tank, on the far side of his central tile. A simple way to think of this is that non-tank players stand on the "mirrored" tile of the tank on the opposite side of the boss: draw a straight line from the tank through the middle of Ocellus' 3x3 area, and any tile along that line beyond the boss receives the bonus.

The bonus is not limited to melee range. It applies anywhere along the line behind Ocellus, so ranged and magic attackers can stand further back and still benefit, as long as they remain in line with the tank. This makes it possible to hit a max of 121 with a Zaryte crossbow special. This bonus is temporarily disabled during the '''Untether''' mechanic.

* '''Tank in the middle of a side:''' players directly opposite, in the middle of the 3 tiles on the other side, deal bonus damage, as do players further back on the same straight line.
* '''Tank at the end of a side (next to a corner):''' when the tank stands on one of the tiles flanking a corner of the boss (the green tiles in the first and third diagrams), the bonus applies to the mirrored tiles beside the opposite corner, plus the diagonal line extending away from that corner.

'''Examples''' (green = tank, orange = tiles that receive the 10% bonus, purple = Ocellus)

